  "name": "probe-feature-flag-state",
  "description": "Probe the runtime state of a named feature flag in a CLI binary. Covers the four-pronged evidence protocol (binary strings, live invocation, on-disk state, platform cache), the four-state classification (LIVE / DARK / INDETERMINATE / UNKNOWN), gate-vs-event disambiguation, conjunction-gate handling, and skill-substitution scenarios where a flag appears DARK but the capability is delivered by other means. Use when verifying whether a documented or inferred capability has rolled out, when auditing dark-launched features, or when a prior probe's conclusions need refreshing against a new binary version.",
